From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ai_re <ai_re@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:10:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] board: CS8210-32X installer build (boot SPI write window)

alpine_v3_cs8210_installer_defconfig: the CS8210 board build, started
from RAM by the vendor U-Boot (loadx + booti), cut down to what writes
our al-boot objects into the boot flash under scheme A'
(devices/cs8210-32x/boot-chain.md section 7, spi-upgrade-plan.md):

- the boot SPI NOR read-only (0019, 0025) except five windows on the
  MX25U25635F (JEDEC c22539, 32 MiB, 4-byte opcodes, patch 0027):
  0x020000+0x1000 (second TOC), 0x030000+0x1000 (BOOT_MODE),
  0x038000+0x8000 (our U-Boot's redundant env, 0x38000/0x3c000),
  0x0f0000+0xa0000 (app slot A), 0x280000+0x100000 (app slot B: past the
  factory U-Boot's data end 0x27808c, over never-run orphans, up to the
  factory env at 0x380000); "sf erase"/"sf write" for them, 4 KiB
  sectors. Stage2, the factory TOC, DT, SerDes firmware, stage3, the
  factory U-Boot, its env and ONIE cannot be erased or programmed by
  this build;
- prompt "cs8210-installer> " (the host tool sends a destructive command
  only after seeing it, never to the vendor prompt), autoboot off;
- console, DRAM, loadx/loady, crc32, md/cmp, PSCI reset; no PCI, SATA,
  I2C, file systems, booti, network, env storage.

Scope: cs8210.
---
 configs/alpine_v3_cs8210_installer_defconfig | 91 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 91 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 configs/alpine_v3_cs8210_installer_defconfig

diff --git a/configs/alpine_v3_cs8210_installer_defconfig b/configs/alpine_v3_cs8210_installer_defconfig
new file mode 100644
